  "anomalies": [],
  "summary": "The drawing is a renumbered build of the m5-pantilt board: reference designators differ from the spec table (e.g. the 2x15 M-BUS connectors are J6/J2 instead of J1/J2, BAT is J1, PortB is J11, 5V_POWER is J10, servo headers are J8/J9, and the SS54/PMEG/MOSFET/PNP/MAX3485 are D3/D1/Q2/Q3/U2), but every functional block, component type, value and count matches the specification (SS54 series diode with the >0.6 V note, PMEG3030EP with the 3A/360 mV note feeding four 100 uF bulk caps, 0.1 uF on the MAX3485 +3V3, 1 k series resistors at the servo signal pins, the 10 k/5.1 k base divider and 47 k gate pull, the 2 k/20 k/2.2 k/2.2 k bias network, DE//RE tied and driven from the PNP, and six 0-ohm jumpers for the PWM-select and serial-bridge functions). The stale assembly note referencing R9/R10/R11 while the drawn jumpers are R15/R2/R19/R10 is a drawing-text mismatch, not an electrical deviation, so no anomaly is reported."
}

